@@ -823,6 +823,12 @@ Does Celery support task priorities?
 **Answer**: Yes, RabbitMQ supports priorities since version 3.5.0,
 and the Redis transport emulates priority support.
 
+In both cases higher numbers mean higher priority: for RabbitMQ (AMQP) a
+higher priority value is processed first, and for Redis the same holds since
+Celery 4.0, where priority 0 is the lowest and 9 is the highest. Before
+Celery 4.0 the Redis ordering was reversed (0 was the highest priority), so
+older guidance suggesting that 0 is the highest priority no longer applies.
+
 You can also prioritize work by routing high priority tasks
 to different workers. In the real world this usually works better
 than per message priorities. You can use this in combination with rate
